    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d382">

                <pb facs="0377" n="369" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg369"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.51/1543: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-08-02T14:00:00-03:00">August 2, 1939—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 1:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>236. My 234, August 1, 4 p.m.<anchor n="31" xml:id="d382-f1"/> Aranha says that
                    the Brazilian Government agrees to pay Munro’s expenses but confidentially
                    trusts that his expenses will not reach anything like $7500, a figure which they
                    consider exorbitant. Aranha repeats that Munro should not arrive here earlier
                    than the 13th.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
